 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441861 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186441807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b42f1b9c-fdac-53cf-8a66-7baeb416267b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441832 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186441848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186441848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441862 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f3558260-62d0-5d33-bce8-4cbce9cd5b5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/53/53f7fa21d70601517c90f19f1b15c4a92ba53d6ecfa685a17174e5fe5394ab8b.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(-4,4)$  and $(-4,6)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "059dbb93-56f4-55ee-894b-e3361b03f75b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186441863 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $2$ units, so the distance equals $2.$\n\n![](images/67/6759fd05bd968e4e3eb994ea05214eb344b57b3bc4c74502a4a3fbbca5602127.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then